OL,3,GNEWSAGuard boats move into position as
OL,4,Aexperts deal with unexploded WW2 bomb
OL,5,Afound in docks
OL,6,
OL,7,FAbout 2,000 people from more than 300
OL,8,Fhomes in Falmouth have been evacuated
OL,9,Fas experts deal with a World War Two
OL,10,Fbomb
OL,12,FEmergency services were initially
OL,13,Fcalled to Falmouth Docks at 09:15 BST
OL,14,Fon Monday after the suspected 250lb
OL,15,F(115kg) American World War Two
OL,16,Fair-dropped device was found in the
OL,17,Fwater
OL,19,FA 300m (984ft) exclusion zone was
OL,20,Fpreviously in place which has since
OL,21,Fbeen expanded to 755m (2,477ft)
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
